  "solution": {
    "approach": "The required sum is constant (4 + 8 = 12). For each test case we simply output 12. The algorithm reads the integer T and repeats printing 12 exactly T times. This runs in O(T) time and O(1) extra space.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(T) total, where T is the number of test cases.",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) auxiliary space.",
    "code": {
      "C": "",
      "C++": "",
      "Java": "import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String line = br.readLine();\n        int T = Integer.parseInt(line.trim());\n        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();\n        for (int i = 0; i < T; i++) {\n            sb.append(12);\n            if (i + 1 < T) sb.append('\\n');\n        }\n        System.out.print(sb.toString());\n    }\n}",
      "Python3": "",
      "JavaScript": ""
    },
